- API/Influx success ≠ portal UI; WP gateway registry + Influx constants both required
- Live debug is Debug Log Manager path in `WP_DEBUG_LOG`, not `wp-content/debug.log`
- Hetzner host: `dedivirt3789.your-server.de`, FTP `ampxapp`, PHP 8.4

#### Session 9: Shared API Key Auth (August 2026)
- ✅ Local `/api/v2/` requires `X-AmpX-Api-Key` (`AMPX_API_KEY` in config; `hash_equals` gate in `v2/index.php`)
- ✅ Firmware `ampxportal_api_key` + header in `postToAmpXPortal2()`; `FIRMWARE_VERSION` **1.0.3**
- ✅ Verified curl + Postman: 401 without/unchecked key, 201 with correct key on `ampx-app.local`
- ⏳ Live Hetzner not yet gated — deploy API + flash/OTA together to avoid production 401s

**Key Learnings**:
- Smallest fleet-prep change is shared API secret before scale; per-gateway keys can reuse same header later
- Postman must have the key header **checked** or the request is unauthenticated
- Do not put real secrets in public README examples (`YOUR_KEY` placeholder only)

#### Session 10: Portal Meter Data UX (August 2026)
- ✅ Theme `ampx-portal-theme` **1.0.9**: meter-data table horizontal scroll — `max-height` on `.table-wrapper` so H-scrollbar stays in viewport
- ✅ Plugin `ampx-portal-plugin` **1.1.4**: display newest **1000** / last **30 days**; UI copy states limits; Export CSV = full 30d via `admin_post_ampx_export_meter_csv`
- ✅ Verified local gateway **100008** / SN **3423875005**; CLI `bin/test-meter-export-limits.php`
- ⏳ Live Hetzner still needs theme + plugin deploy for the UX fixes

**Key Learnings**:
- `overflow: hidden` on `.table-wrapper` clips wide tables with no scrollbar
- Horizontal scrollbar at the bottom of a multi-thousand-px table is effectively invisible — constrain height
- DOM-based CSV export cannot serve “all data” once the table is capped — use server export with `$limit = null`

#### Session 11: InfluxDB Cloud Serverless org (August 2026)
- ✅ Created managed **Cloud Serverless** account **AmpX**, org **Energy Gateway** (`86a141bfd8d7f66a`)
- ✅ Region AWS **eu-central-1** (Frankfurt); host `https://eu-central-1-1.aws.cloud2.influxdata.com`
- ✅ Bucket **`energy_metrics`** (ID `43bdc9cfa0531940`, 30-day retention)
- ✅ Decision: managed Serverless (not self-host Influx on Hetzner); company email for org ownership
- ✅ API token → `INFLUXDB_CLOUD_*` in local `api/config/config.php` only
- ✅ Spike: write **204**; InfluxQL **200** after DBRP; script `api/v2/tests/spike_cloud_serverless.php`
- ⏳ Not wired to AmpX yet — production remains `influxdb2.ampx.app` until API v3 + portal cutover
- Note: **InfluxDB 3 Cloud** (early-access managed Enterprise) ≠ **Cloud Serverless**

**Key Learnings**:
- Prefer Cloud Serverless for SQL + low ops; escalate to Cloud Dedicated if quotas bite
- Rough cost at 200 gateways × 30s posts is material — longer upload intervals cut Serverless spend sharply
- Keep Influx tokens out of git/docs; org metadata (host/org id) is fine to document

